data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":619,"item_id":"msg_0b997f21622732db016b02f950ab6887d1a2ee71db3c06804a","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"birch-4\",\"decision\":\"reuse\",\"ability\":\"weather-lean-to\",\"reason\":\"The implemented weather-lean-to provides the requested physical wind and rain protection with actual materials, construction effort, shared geometry and exposure effects. Birch-4 has not mastered it and owns roots, not demonstrated construction supplies. Neither materials nor an existing shelter are granted by this review; missing supplies do not require a different capability.\",\"specification\":\"Reuse weather-lean-to's existing public schema and execution contract unchanged; consult its full contract for operation parameters. Individual learning takes 4 rounds. Construction requires 4 branch, 2 vine and 6 bark, a valid clear dry 2×2 site with a 0.8 entrance, and 8 work rounds costing 2 energy each. Ordinary moist soil is not automatically a valid dry site: validate actual site conditions. The result is an oriented traversable roof supported by three physical posts; enforce existing collision, entrance and full-body roof coverage checks. Rain reduction is 0.8×integrity and wind reduction 0.6×integrity, feeding actual wetness, thermal and rest calculations rather than automatic comfort. Wear per round is 0.0005+0.002×rain+0.002×wind. Repair requires 1 bark and 0.5 vine, 2 rounds at 2 energy, and restores 0.25 integrity subject to the existing cap. Preserve existing start/progress/pause/completion/cancellation, remaining-work, component provenance and escrow-ownership rules; death cancels work without duplicating or deleting escrow. No simulation time passes during this review, and no shelter, supplies or mastery are created.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Construction, ownership, requesting and learning award no wellbeing. Reuse the existing actual-weather-refuge source, without an alias: successful sheltered-rest events from rest apply only to the actor who independently completes genuinely beneficial rest under actual protective coverage. Its temporary feedback is 0.3, capped at 0.6, held for 4 rounds, with refresh repetition and an 8-round cooldown. Its maintained component gains 0.015 per qualifying sheltered-rest event, caps at 0.4 and decays by 0.003 per round without qualifying maintenance. Reduced exposure must produce real physical relief; benign conditions or already fully recovered rest do not qualify merely because a roof exists. Preserve the existing practice-confirmed rule only for its already-defined qualified paid-practice milestones, never mastery or duplicate rewards. Health, nutrition and protected mental accounts remain independent.\",\"visualReview\":\"Use the existing shelter rendering: oriented roof, three collidable posts, traversable covered area and entrance, with actual construction progress and integrity represented. Bind exposure feedback to the declared shelter-exposure event and completed beneficial rest to sheltered-rest; retain existing process-progress, process-completed and process-stopped bindings for work replay. Show only actual paid progress, components and measured protection, not a completed shelter preview presented as an existing object.\",\"learning\":4}]}","logprobs":[]}

